    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.66), whose elite 0.474 xwOBA against Walbert Ure\u00f1a makes him our most potent start. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Trea Turner** (75.43) also project as foundational pieces, benefiting from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near 4.84. **Kyle Schwarber** (71.62) rounds out our top-tier targets, leveraging a strong park factor and top-of-the-order positioning. **Colt Keith** (63.38) is our standout 1B play; his projection is bolstered by a significant platoon advantage and a high batting order slot, ensuring he remains a priority despite the 33% rain risk at the stadium.\n\nStrategic volatility is centered on the bottom of our lineup and bench. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.12) earns the start despite a negative platoon split against Matthew Liberatore, as his lead-off spot remains vital for our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases. **Casey Schmitt** (57.76) and **Nelson Velazquez** (55.53) provide steady secondary production, with **Casey Schmitt** specifically benefiting from a positive dynamic platoon adjustment against Brandon Sproat. The most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (48.47), who narrowly missed the cut; while his platoon splits were favorable, he lacked the explosive categorical upside of our middle infielders. Finally, managers should monitor the weather in the Bradish start, which threatens the availability of both **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**, and keep an eye on lineup confirmations for **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Carson Benge**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to ensure these projected scores hold against official team cards.",
